# Build context exclusions.
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ONE IS *.tsbuildinfo. tsconfig.base.json sets
# `incremental: true`, so TypeScript records what it has already emitted. Copy a
# stale buildinfo into the image WITHOUT the dist it describes — which is
# exactly what happens when dist is excluded and buildinfo is not — and `tsc`
# exits 0 having emitted nothing at all. The image then builds an application
# with no compiled output, and the first error is a wall of "Cannot find module
# '@nexuspuppet/contracts'" that points nowhere near the cause.
#
# This only ever bit a build from a checkout where someone had run
# `npm run build` locally; CI and the VM clone fresh, which is why it went
# unnoticed. Found by building the images from a working tree.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/dist
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/coverage

.git
.github
e2e/.results
qa-report*

# NOT excluded: packages/enterprise. A private build needs it in the context —
# see the four edits documented at the top of apps/api/Dockerfile.
